{"status":"Error","code":"InvalidParameter","error":"The Reservations domain is turned off for this company. Turn it on from Inventory Setup.","nextStep":"Ask an administrator with the Inv. Posting Gate permission set to turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page. Data.Records.Set cannot change this setup.","hint":"For usage details, call the \"Help.Implementation.Get\" message type with subject \"Inventory.Reservation.Create\". Always read the help before calling a message type."}

--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "subject": {
      "use": "notUsed",
      "forms": [],
      "description": "The source line is named in data (sourceType, sourceNo and sourceLineNo); subject is not read."
    },
    "dataRequired": true,
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json"
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "data.sourceType + data.sourceSubtype + data.sourceNo + data.sourceLineNo",
      "form": "table no., subtype, document no. and line no.",
      "description": "The source line to reserve for: a Sales Line (sourceType 37), Purchase Line (39), Transfer Line (5741) or Assembly Line (901). sourceSubtype is the document type ordinal, or the transfer direction (0 outbound, 1 inbound), and defaults to 1 for sales, purchase and assembly lines and to 0 for a transfer line."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "sourceType",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Source table number: 37 Sales Line, 39 Purchase Line, 5741 Transfer Line, 901 Assembly Line."
    },
    {
      "name": "sourceSubtype",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Source subtype: the sales, purchase or assembly document type ordinal (1 = Order), or the transfer direction (0 outbound, 1 inbound). Defaults to 1 for sales, purchase and assembly and 0 for transfer lines."
    },
    {
      "name": "sourceNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Source document number."
    },
    {
      "name": "sourceLineNo",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Source document line number."
    },
    {
      "name": "quantity",
      "type": "number",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Quantity to reserve, in the source line unit of measure. Greater than 0."
    },
    {
      "name": "itemNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Optional item number; must match the source line when sent."
    },
    {
      "name": "locationCode",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Optional location code; must match the source line location when sent."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success when at least one reservation entry was created."
      },
      {
        "name": "entryNo",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "First created reservation entry number. Pass it to Inventory.Reservation.Cancel."
      },
      {
        "name": "entryNos",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "All created reservation entry numbers (one per reserved supply)."
      },
      {
        "name": "itemNo",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Item number of the source line."
      },
      {
        "name": "locationCode",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Location code of the source line; blank when the line has none."
      },
      {
        "name": "quantity",
        "type": "decimal",
        "description": "Quantity reserved by this call, in the source line unit of measure."
      },
      {
        "name": "requestedQuantity",
        "type": "decimal",
        "description": "The quantity that was asked for, as sent."
      },
      {
        "name": "fullAutoReservation",
        "type": "boolean",
        "description": "True when the full requested quantity was reserved."
      },
      {
        "name": "sourceType",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "The source table number, as sent."
      },
      {
        "name": "sourceSubtype",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "The source subtype that was used, including the default."
      },
      {
        "name": "sourceNo",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The source document number, in upper case."
      },
      {
        "name": "sourceLineNo",
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "The source line number, as sent."
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "when": "sourceType, sourceNo, sourceLineNo or quantity is missing.",
      "fix": "Name the source table, document, line and the quantity to reserve."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "sourceType, sourceSubtype or sourceLineNo is not a whole number of 0 or more, quantity is not a number, or sourceNo, itemNo or locationCode is not text within 20, 20 and 10 characters (sourceNo must not be blank).",
      "fix": "Send the integers as JSON numbers and the codes as JSON strings within their length."
    },
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "when": "The source line does not exist.",
      "fix": "Check sourceType, sourceSubtype, sourceNo and sourceLineNo."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "Unsupported sourceType or sourceSubtype, quantity not above 0, or itemNo/locationCode differ from the source line.",
      "fix": "Correct the indicated parameter."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "The source line is not an item line, or the Reservations domain is turned off for the company.",
      "fix": "Reserve for an item line, or turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "when": "No supply is available, so nothing was reserved.",
      "fix": "Check inventory or incoming supply at the source location, then retry."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The caller cannot change reservation entries.",
      "fix": "Assign Bifrost Full Access (extended by Inventory write permissions) and a Business Central permission set that can change reservation entries."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "The native reservation error text.",
      "when": "Business Central refuses the reservation while it runs; the answer carries its text.",
      "fix": "Read the error text and correct the source line or the supply it names."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "when": "The sales source item or line cannot be reserved: non-inventory item, Reserve Never, drop shipment, special order or missing shipment date.",
      "fix": "Correct the source line reservation settings and retry."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "write",
    "changes": "Creates reservation entries that tie the source line to available supply, and commits them when the call finishes. Nothing is posted; the source documents and the ledger entries stay as they are.",
    "idempotent": false,
    "permissionSet": "Bifrost Full Access",
    "preconditions": [
      "The Reservations domain is turned on in Inventory Setup.",
      "The source line exists and is an item line that has supply to reserve from."
    ],
    "writes": true,
    "posts": false
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Read reservations before creating one."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.Cancel",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Cancel a reservation instead of creating one."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reservation.AutoReserve",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Reserve the whole outstanding quantity of a sales order line without naming a quantity; it reserves all or nothing."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.OrderTracking.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Read which supply is tracked against the source line after reserving."
    }
  ],
  "workflow": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reservation.Get",
        "purpose": "Read the reservations that already exist before reserving."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reservation.Create",
        "purpose": "Reserve supply for the source line and keep entryNo from the answer."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.OrderTracking.Get",
        "purpose": "Read which supply is now tracked against the line."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reservation.Cancel",
        "purpose": "Cancel a reservation by its entryNo when it is no longer wanted."
      }
    ]
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Reserve 5 units for sales order line 10000. Replace the identifiers with your own.",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.Reservation.Create",
        "data": {
          "sourceType": 37,
          "sourceSubtype": 1,
          "sourceNo": "S-ORD101001",
          "sourceLineNo": 10000,
          "quantity": 5
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "entryNo": 120,
        "entryNos": [
          120
        ],
        "itemNo": "1000",
        "locationCode": "BLUE",
        "quantity": 5,
        "requestedQuantity": 5,
        "fullAutoReservation": true,
        "sourceType": 37,
        "sourceSubtype": 1,
        "sourceNo": "S-ORD101001",
        "sourceLineNo": 10000
      }
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Reserves supply for one real source line with the same automatic reservation as the Auto Reserve action and returns the reservation entry numbers.",
  "notes": "Sales source lines use the same item/line eligibility as AutoReserve: inventory items only, neither item nor line Reserve set to Never, no drop shipment or special order, and a shipment date is required. Auto Reserve picks the supply, as the Auto Reserve action does, and reserves at most the requested quantity. A partial reservation still answers Success with fullAutoReservation false; when nothing is available the answer is PreconditionFailed and nothing is written. quantity is in the unit of measure of the source line. sourceNo, itemNo and locationCode are converted to upper case; itemNo and locationCode only check the source line. sourceSubtype defaults to 1 (Order) for sales, purchase and assembly lines and to 0 (outbound) for a transfer line. Bifrost commits the reservation when the call finishes; under Omit Commit the caller's transaction commits instead. Read reservations with Inventory.Reservation.Get and cancel an entry with Inventory.Reservation.Cancel."
}

## Errors and warnings
An error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.
When a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.
Request values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.
Request values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `"1234.56"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.
Answers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.
Both success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.
`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {"type":"Memory.User.Set","strict":true,"data":{"memory":"test","memry":"typo"}} is refused.
`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.
Feature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.
A message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.
`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is "no concurrent lock on the same records"; `nextStep` is "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed." Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.
Codes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.
